summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Left elbow pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Anna Brown is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with left elbow pain.

The patient reports that she has been having joint pain. She states that she sits at her desk a lot for work and type and stay in a fixed position all day. After work, it is hard for her to open and close her left elbow. She has noticed some swelling on the tip of her elbow. She is right-handed. She is able to write, which is good, but typing is difficult. She denies numbness or tingling in her hands. She denies any weakness in her arm. She denies any fever or chills.

Regarding her epilepsy, she states that she has not had any recent seizures. She is still taking Keppra. She notes that her last seizure was a year ago.

The patient notes that she is doing well with her depression therapy. She notes that she still feels a little down and stressed. She denies any suicidal or homicidal ideation.

Regarding her peptic ulcer disease, she states that she did have a lot of stress a year ago, and she was having some issues. We did an endoscopy which showed gastritis, and she was placed on Protonix. She is doing better now. She denies any issues with this.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fever, chills.
• Musculoskeletal: Endorses left elbow pain.
• Neurological: Denies numbness or tingling in her hands. Denies weakness in her arm.
• ENT: Endorses nasal congestion.

PHYSICAL EXAMINATION

• Musculoskeletal: Examination of the left elbow: Erythema and edema of the left elbow. Pain with palpation of the left olecranon. Warm to palpation. Pain with flexion and extension of the left elbow. Palpable right radial pulse.

RESULTS

X-rays of the left arm were obtained. There is no evidence of any elbow fracture.

Endoscopy was performed and showed gastritis.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Anna Brown is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with left elbow pain.

Olecranon bursitis.
• Medical Reasoning: She has left elbow pain. She states that she sits at her desk a lot for work and type and stay in a fixed position all day. After work, it is hard for her to open and close her left elbow. She has noticed some swelling on the tip of her elbow. She is right-handed. She is able to write, which is good, but typing is difficult. She denies numbness or tingling in her hands. She denies any weakness in her arm. She denies any fever or chills. She has erythema and edema of her left elbow. She has pain with palpation of her left olecranon. She is warm to palpation. She has pain with flexion and extension of her left elbow. There is a palpable right radial pulse. X-rays of her left arm were obtained and did not show any evidence of a fracture.
• Medical Treatment: We will have her use a pillow to support her elbow. We will give her some meloxicam 15 mg, once a day. She can ice the area.

Epilepsy.
• Medical Reasoning: She has not had any recent seizures. She is still taking Keppra. Her last seizure was a year ago.
• Medical Treatment: We will continue with the Keppra 500 mg, twice a day. She needs a refill.

Depression.
• Medical Reasoning: She is doing well with her therapy and does not want to take medication.
• Medical Treatment: We will start her on Lexapro 10 mg, once a day.

Peptic ulcer disease.
• Medical Reasoning: She did have a lot of stress a year ago and was having some issues. We did an endoscopy which showed gastritis. She was placed on Protonix.
• Medical Treatment: She will continue Protonix 40 mg, once a day before meals.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
