summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Full spectrum STD testing.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Grace Ross is a 24-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum STD testing. She reports symptoms of discomfort, change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She states that the right side of her vagina is becoming painful. She denies any fevers or chills. She recently learned that her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people and wants to be evaluated for all STDs.

Ms. Ross is currently asymptomatic. She started noticing some abnormal discharge last week. She also reports that the discharge smells different and is not the same color or consistency as it has been previously. She also notes that the right side of her vagina has become sore and this has not gone away.

Ms. Ross has been dating her partner for 3 years. She states that she is not sure when her partner started cheating on her, but believes it may have been 3 months ago. She has had one irregular pap smear in the past, which was 20 years ago. She has not had one since then. Her last pap smear was 6 months ago and was normal.

MEDICAL HISTORY

Patient reports history of abnormal pap smear.

SOCIAL HISTORY

Patient reports she is employed as a full-time teacher. She reports that she has been dating her partner for 3 years.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Denies fevers or chills.
Gynecologic: Reports abnormal discharge, odor, and right vaginal pain.

PHYSICAL EXAM

General: Patient is alert and oriented, in no acute distress.
Pelvic Exam: No external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge with normal color and smell. Cervix is normal. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness. No adnexal tenderness or masses noted. Swabs were done for STD testing.

RESULTS

Pending.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Screen for STD.
• Medical Reasoning: Patient is high risk due to abnormal pap smear in the past and recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners for some period of time.
• Patient Education and Counseling: We discussed the importance of safe sex practices and the risks associated with her partner’s infidelity. We discussed that it is important to get tested regularly for STDs, especially given her history of abnormal pap smears.
• Medical Treatment: We obtained swabs for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis. We also obtained blood for syphilis, HIV, and hepatitis C. Some of these tests will take longer than others. We will call her if we see anything abnormal, but she can call us in 3 days for results if she has not heard from us.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan. }}<|eot_id|>
