summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Right knee injury.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

The patient is a 28-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for an evaluation of a right knee injury. The patient states that he was playing soccer over the weekend and went to go out and kick the ball and felt a pop in his right knee. This occurred 3 days ago. He states that he noticed some swelling, which has since decreased. He reports that his knee is not as functional as it used to be. He states that he is having pain that is ranging from 6 to 7 out of 10. He denies taking anything for the pain other than ibuprofen, which he has been taking on a regular basis. He reports that he is able to bend his knee but it hurts towards the end of the motion. He denies being able to fully straighten his knee without pain. He states that he is able to bear weight on the knee but it feels loose.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Musculoskeletal: Reports right knee pain and swelling.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Musculoskeletal: Examination of the right knee reveals significant effusion. Slight ecchymosis is noted. Pain to palpation on the medial joint line. Positive Lachman test. Muscle strength of 5/5 bilaterally in the lower extremities. Neurovascularly intact distally.

ASSESSMENT

Right knee anterior cruciate ligament tear.

PLAN

After reviewing the patient's examination and radiographic findings today, I have had a lengthy discussion with the patient in regards to his current symptoms. I have recommended that we obtain an MRI of the right knee to evaluate the integrity of the ACL. I have also recommended that we obtain a CBC to rule out infection. I have prescribed Meloxicam 50 mg once daily for pain and inflammation. I have also recommended that he use ice and a knee immobilizer. Additionally, he should use crutches when ambulating. I have advised him to limit his activities, including his work activities. He should also avoid jogging until further notice. All questions were answered.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up with me once the MRI results are available. }}<|eot_id|>
